# gnome-session -- the session manager that starts gnome-shell and the rest of
# the desktop, and decides what "logging in" actually runs.
#
# GNOME 48 series, BLFS 12.4, which pins 48.0.
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/gnome-session/48/gnome-session-48.0.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=dd909fbc5b22cdbdb2fc4df1a47d78d1b5943ccc5e61e6a20a1846246347c417
SRC_DIR=gnome-session-48.0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# -Dsystemduserunitdir IS NOT OPTIONAL AND BLFS'S VALUE MUST NOT BE COPIED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# There is NO option to stop building the systemd user units. meson.build:117-121
# reads the option and, IF IT IS EMPTY, resolves the directory by asking
# pkg-config for systemd:
#
#     if systemd_userunitdir == ''
#       systemd_dep = dependency('systemd', version: '>= 242', required: true)
#
# elogind ships libelogind.pc and a libsystemd.pc SYMLINK but NO systemd.pc --
# established three times over in this tree, in NetworkManager, ModemManager and
# accountsservice. So leaving this option empty is a hard configure failure.
#
# ONE OPTION, TWO UNRELATED JOBS: setting it both chooses where the units go AND
# is the only thing that prevents that dependency('systemd') lookup from
# running. Anyone "simplifying" this flag away breaks the build in a way that
# names systemd rather than naming this line.
#
# BLFS PASSES -D systemduserunitdir=/tmp AND THAT IS WRONG FOR A PACKAGER.
# On a live system /tmp is a fine place to throw units nothing will read. Under
# a DESTDIR staged build it becomes $DESTDIR/tmp, and tape would then PACKAGE
# those files as /tmp/... entries -- a package owning paths under /tmp, which
# nothing in this tree has ever done. It is a book instruction that is correct
# for the book's audience and wrong here, and nothing about the command says so.
#
# So the units are pointed at their natural location and REMOVED in install.sh,
# which is the same idiom gnome-shell and evolution-data-server already use --
# three packages, one assertion, /usr/lib/systemd absent from all of them.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# libsystemd CANNOT BE DECLINED HERE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# meson.build:124 is
#
#     libsystemd_dep = dependency('libsystemd', version: '>= 209', required: true)
#
# unconditional, no option, no guard. It resolves against elogind's libsystemd.pc
# symlink -- and that is how an elogind system is expected to build, so it is
# accepted rather than fought. The consequence is that ELOGIND IS A RUNTIME
# DEPENDENCY OF THIS PACKAGE, declared because the artefact links it and not
# because the build file names it.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# -Dx11=false, and what it does NOT stop installing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# It drops ice, sm, x11 and xtrans (meson.build:88-92, :103-109). This tree's
# mutter is built -Dx11=false with Xwayland only, so an X session is not
# something this desktop can offer.
#
# IT DOES NOT STOP THE XSESSIONS ENTRY. data/meson.build:52-66 sends the plain
# 'gnome' desktop file to xsessions through an `else` branch that no option
# guards -- the x11 test only picks a DIFFERENT directory for names ending in
# -xorg. So a build with X11 support off still advertises an X11 session to the
# display manager. install.sh removes it, because an offered session that cannot
# start is worse than one that is not offered.
#
# The Wayland entry survives that removal by an upstream accident worth knowing:
# meson.build:146-148 passes have_x11 to meson_post_install.py as the STRING
# 'false', and the script does `have_x11 = bool(sys.argv[2])` -- and bool('false')
# is True in Python. So the script copies xsessions/gnome.desktop into
# wayland-sessions unconditionally, which is the file gdm reads to offer this
# session at all. install.sh asserts it rather than trusting a bug to keep
# behaving; if upstream ever fixes that line, this package stops offering a
# session and nothing else changes.
#
# -Dman=false and -Ddocbook=false: both default TRUE and want xmlto and the
# DocBook stylesheets, neither packaged. BLFS turns both off here as well.
#
# NOT SET, deliberately:
#
#   -Dsession_selector  already false; it is a GTK dialog for choosing between
#                       sessions, and this tree offers one.
#   -Ddeprecation_flags already false; a compiler-warning switch.
MESON_ARGS="-Dx11=false -Dman=false -Ddocbook=false -Dsystemduserunitdir=/usr/lib/systemd/user"
